--on the East slopes of the Himalayas
1: वा. 1. १८९; ४१. ४३-6; ४७, ४७.
noted for great sages.
2: भा. X. ८७. 7.
Residence of Manu. Here देवापि [and Puru (Manu) वि। प्।] continued their योग practice. These yogins would start the course of वर्णाश्रम धर्म again at the end of Kali;
3: IX. १२. 6; २२. १७;

(III)--a southern kingdom of मध्यदेश unfit for श्राद्ध; a Janapada of the दक्षिणापथ. Its king was stationed by जरासन्ध on the east gate of मथुरा, and on the same direction during the siege of Gomanta;
1: Br. II. १६. ४२ & ५७; III. १३. १३; १४. ३३ & ८०; ७४. १९८ & २१३; M. १६३. ७२; वा. ७७. १३; ७८. २३; ९९. ३२४, ३८६, ४०२.
present at [page१-333+ ४६] Pradyumna's marriage. Advised Rukmin to vanquish बलराम in dice, and laughed at the latter when he was defeated. His teeth were broken by राम.
